<article class="env-lemma" id="00KG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00KG">Lemma <span data-tag="00KG">10.60.4</span>.</a> The Krull dimension of $R$ is the supremum of the heights of its (maximal) primes. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is so because we can always add a maximal ideal at the end of a chain of prime ideals. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>